<title>USA: Parker lands 5-Year Kazakhstan contract.</title>
<headline>Parker lands 5-Year Kazakhstan contract.</headline>
<dateline>TULSA, Okla. 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Parker Drilling Co said Tuesday it has received a five-year contract to expand operations in Kazakhstan.</p>
<p>The new agreement creates a broad alliance between Parker and Tengizchevroil, the developing operator of the Tengiz Oil Field, the drilling company said.</p>
<p>Tengizchevroil is a joint venture between the Republic of Kazakhstan, Chevron Corp and Mobil Corp.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
</text>
